<Layout title="About Tarian Ventures" description="Meet Dan Winder and the purpose behind Tarian Ventures: a founder-led business based in Wales, exploring opportunities across markets.">
  <PageIntro label="About us" title="A home for ideas worth testing."><p>Tarian Ventures is a founder-led venture development company based in Wales.</p><p>It provides space to explore ideas across technology, infrastructure and complex regulated markets. Tarian Compute is our current priority, alongside the continued development of AltGRC and investigation of new opportunities.</p></PageIntro>
  <section class="section tint-section"><div class="shell split"><div><img class="about-shield" src="/brand/logos/tarian-mark-green.svg" alt="" width="100" height="100" /><h2>Built in Wales.<br />Looking outward.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p class="lead">Tarian takes its name from the Welsh word for shield.</p><p>Our roots are in Wales, but our ambitions and the markets we investigate extend well beyond it.</p><p>We are particularly interested in opportunities where technology intersects with infrastructure, resilience and significant market change.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section shell split" id="founder"><div><p class="eyebrow">Founder</p><h2>Dan Winder</h2></div><div class="prose"><p class="lead">Dan brings experience spanning technology delivery, governance, data, digital risk and enterprise transformation.</p><p>His career has included work across telecommunications, government services and regulated consumer businesses, alongside the development of independent technology ventures.</p><p>These disciplines inform Tarian’s work: considering commercial opportunity alongside operational constraints, risk and the practical requirements of delivery.</p><p>Today, that work includes early exploration through Tarian Compute and the continued development of AltGRC.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Start a conversation with Dan <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
</Layout>
